    {
      "text": "she called his name Judah, Gen. 29:35. Judah … thy father’s children shall bow down, Gen. 49:8. sceptre shall not depart from Judah, Gen. 49:10. this is the blessing of Judah, Deut. 33:7. David was king in Hebron over the house of Judah, 2 Sam. 2:11. none left but the tribe of Judah, 2 Kgs. 17:18. Judah prevailed above his brethren, 1 Chr. 5:2. Lord carried away Judah and Jerusalem, 1 Chr. 6:15. chosen Judah to be the ruler, 1 Chr. 28:4. vision of Isaiah … concerning Judah and Jerusalem, Isa. 1:1. from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah, Isa. 7:17 (2 Ne. 17:17). Ephraim, Manasseh … shall be against Judah, Isa. 9:21 (2 Ne. 19:21). Ephraim shall not envy Judah, and Judah shall not vex, Isa. 11:13 (2 Ne. 21:13). say unto the cities of Judah, Behold your God, Isa. 40:9. make a new covenant with … Judah, Jer. 31:31 (Heb. 8:8). one stick … For Judah, Ezek. 37:16 (37:15–17). Lord shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, Zech. 2:12. ten men shall take hold … of the skirt of … a Jew, Zech. 8:23.",
